# AI Contribution Log: SLE-4



## 1. AI tools used

I used Claude (Anthropic) to help draft the ADR, the README and this log for SLE-4. In SLE-1, SLE-2 and SLE-3 I used ChatGPT for support, as already recorded in those reports.

## 2. How AI helped

**Understanding the task.** Claude read the SLE-4 guideline and explained what an ADR is and what the final submission must contain. I gave it my SLE-2 and SLE-3 documents as input.

**Choosing the decision.** Claude analysed my SLE-2 profiling report and my SLE-3 C4 design and suggested the decision to record: BFS as the default search strategy, with A* and the Manhattan heuristic kept as an alternative inside the Search Engine.

**Writing the ADR.** Claude drafted the Context, Decision, Alternatives Considered, Rationale and Consequences sections in the format required by the guideline. It also drafted the short summary of my SLE-1 to SLE-4 journey and the five viva preparation points.

**Presenting the evidence.** Claude arranged my SLE-2 results into a comparison and worked out the percentages used in the rationale: A* was about 17% slower in the average case, about 1.9 times slower in the worst case, and expanded about 40% fewer nodes in the average case.

**Files and formatting.** Claude created the Word document, the README and this log.

## 3. What I did myself

**Earlier SLE work.** I did the work behind the evidence. I implemented BFS and A*, ran the SLE-2 experiments with timeit, node counting and py-spy, recorded the actual measurements, and designed and drew the C4 model in SLE-3.

**Reviewing the decision.** I reviewed the suggested decision against my own results and accepted it as the decision I will defend.

**Verifying the content.** I checked the numbers in the ADR against my SLE-2 report and checked the design points against my SLE-3 container and component diagrams.

**Submission and viva.** I will upload the files to GitHub and Moodle. I will explain and defend the decision, the profiling results and the C4 diagrams in the viva myself, without AI help.

## 4. What the AI did not do

Claude did not run any code or experiments, so all timing and node-count results come from my own SLE-2 work. It did not create any new data, and every number in the ADR is taken from my SLE-2 report. It did not draw my C4 diagrams, which are from my SLE-3 work.

## 5. Declaration

I used AI tools as described above. I understand the decision and can explain the alternatives, the profiling results and the trade-offs. I am responsible for the content I submit and can explain it in the viva.


